-- title:
--   Past $\sigma(\xi_{k1},\dots,\xi_{k,t-1})$ of a row of a triangular array
-- statement:
--   For a triangular array of random vectors $\xi_{kt}$, $1\le t\le k$, the **past of row $k$ before $t$** is the $\sigma$-algebra
--
--   $$
--   \sigma(\xi_{k1},\dots,\xi_{k,t-1})
--   $$
--
--   generated by the earlier entries of the same row (the trivial $\sigma$-algebra when $t=1$). Lemma 6 conditions on it in its martingale-difference condition and in $R_{kt}$.
-- source:
--   Lei, Shanbhag, Variance-Reduced Accelerated First-order Methods: Central Limit Theorems and Confidence Statements, arXiv:2006.07769v3, Lemma 6, p.14

import Mathlib

set_option warn.classDefReducibility false

namespace VRAccelCLT

/-- **The past of a row of a triangular array**, `σ(ξ_{k1}, …, ξ_{k,t−1})`. Lei, Shanbhag,
arXiv:2006.07769v3, Lemma 6, p.14 (the conditioning in `E[· | ξk1, · · · , ξk,t−1]`).

`rowPast ξ k t` is the σ-algebra generated by the random vectors `ξ k s`, `1 ≤ s < t`
(the trivial σ-algebra for `t ≤ 1`).

**Formalization Note.** It is the supremum of the comap σ-algebras of `ξ k s` for `s ∈ [1, t)`
(Borel σ-algebra on `ℝᵐ`). -/
def rowPast {m : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} (ξ : ℕ → ℕ → Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (k t : ℕ) :
    MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ s ∈ Finset.Ico 1 t, MeasurableSpace.comap (ξ k s) inferInstance

end VRAccelCLT


